nuwa only (SM8550 / xnu-8796.141.3): boot progress call sites.

Port of UniXNU/UniXNU-sheng@998d0cc5023d4eff54a1ef40cce6ec89dc10083c
patches/xnu/zzz-boot-progress.patch (git ls-remote verified; MIT per file).
The renderer (package/boot-progress/) is the same commit.

Apply order: after 8796-nuwa-root-auth-skip.patch (bsd_init.c),
8796-nuwa-exec-policy-skip.patch (kern_exec.c) and
UniXNU patches/xnu/native-trust-cache-runtime.patch (startup.c);
the hunks in those three files are anchored on the patched text.
Every call is compiled out unless -DXNU_BOOT_PROGRESS=1.

Dropped hunks (no such site on this base; screen effect):
 * bsd_init.c  sheng_pmgr_run() enter/return stages - no XNU_SHENG_PMGR
   hook here: the "original PMGR nub start/returned" stage rows are
   absent (the PMGR nub is published by the native IOKit route).
 * bsd_init.c  "root authentication decision recorded" - no
   native_owner_root_accepted_checkpoint() call: the nuwa root-auth
   bypass is 8796-nuwa-root-auth-skip, whose stage is already covered by
   "vfs_mountroot mounted; authentication pending".
 * kern_exec.c SystemOS/Data mount stages and the temporary watchdog
   launch policy - XNU_OWNER_*_MOUNT/sheng_boot_watchdog_policy are
   sheng only: no "SystemOS mount"/"Data mount"/watchdog stage rows.
 * sleh.c      boot_progress_user_abort() - no
   user_fault_in_self_restrict_mode() site; boot_progress_user_breakpoint()
   is reverted too (see below).
 * kern_exit.c process-hook exit capture: boot_progress_critical_exit() and
   the 1024-byte prefix_str_buf belong to the sheng fault probe
   (BootFaultProbe.c), which is not built: no CAPTURED rows; the exit
   banner still shows every exit through boot_progress_exit().
 * osfmk/kern/Makefile XNU_ONLY_EXPORTS - the header is not installed;
   the isolated build puts it on the include path instead.

Re-anchored hunks: sleh.c include (8796 copyright line), kern_exit.c
boot_progress_exit() into proc_prepareexit (8796 has the
p_crash_behavior check there, not after a proc_task() line), kern_exec.c
"exec MAC policy REFUSED" into the refusing block left by the exec skip.
Dropped for the same reason as sleh.c: boot_progress_user_breakpoint().

